{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Instance Property","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"externalID":"s:7IvorMXL10MXLBarlineV5levelAA8MXLLevelVSgvp","title":"level","symbolKind":"property","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"level","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLLevelV","text":"MXLLevel","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline\/level"},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"level","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLLevelV","text":"MXLLevel","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLevel"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to a nested MusicXML "},{"code":"<level>","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" element."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"abstract":[{"text":"The level element specifies editorial information for different MusicXML elements. It is defined within a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"group due to its multiple uses within the MusicXML schema.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbarline\/level"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline"]]},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLBarline":{"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"If a barline is other than a normal single barline, it should be represented by a barline type that describes"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"it. This includes information about repeats and multiple endings, as well as line style. Barline data is on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the same level as the other musical data in a score — a child of a measure in a partwise score, or a part in a"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"timewise score. This allows for barlines within measures, as in dotted barlines that subdivide measures in"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"complex meters. The two fermata elements allow for fermatas on both sides of the barline (the lower one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inverted)."}],"title":"MXLBarline","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlbarline","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLBarline","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLBarline","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLBarline"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLLevel":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLLevel"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLLevel"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxllevel","role":"symbol","title":"MXLLevel","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLLevel","type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The level type is used to specify editorial information for different MusicXML elements. The content contains","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"identifying and\/or descriptive text about the editorial status of the parent element.","type":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","url":"\/documentati